      "writtenOn": "2020-08-03T16:04:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this have to vary with our port partner revision (ex. retry 3 times when talking to a PD 2.0 partner)?  Or is it okay to only retry twice when we\u0027re talking to a lower revision partner?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4761,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4765,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "a5df1c029210d6843c21a2fd3b401df9a0f77402",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "741c9223_359d3635",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 4765,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-04T23:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are being very strict, then I think we would need to use the retry count based on the PD revision.... but the GRL compliance test doesn\u0027t require 3 retries for PD 2.0; it allows 2 or 3 retires for a passing result.\n\nThis is because the first version of PD 2.0 actually said the retry count should be 2, then later version of PD 2.0 bump the retry count to 3.  PD 3.0 went back to retry count of 2. The PD 3.0 compliance test does however assert that you only perform exactly 2 retry attempts though.\n\nSo a value of 2 retry attempts will pass both PD 2.0 and PD 3.0 compliance tests. I kept 3 for PD 2.0 to keep is the same as before (and to me an extra retry won\u0027t hurt).\n\nIf this doesn\u0027t feel right, I could be convinced to just reduce the RETRY_COUNT to 2 for everyone. Let me know what your thoughts are!",
      "parentUuid": "3b58dfb4_e1e1137a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4761,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4765,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "a5df1c029210d6843c21a2fd3b401df9a0f77402",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
